  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating App Design**\n\nI\'m starting the process of designing this app. The user wants screens that match a specific design, so I\'ll prioritize visual fidelity. Hotlinking images is an option. I\'ve begun reviewing the available skillsets, focusing on app creation and resource integration, but I need to decide which skill is most critical.\n\n\n**Defining App Functionality**\n\nI\'m now determining the app\'s core features. While the user\'s design is key, the provided features are broad. I\'m prioritizing Firebase integration, user authentication with OAuth, and Google Maps Platform integration for location features. PWA integration and real-time/multi-user functionality are also crucial. I\'m also considering workspace and Gemini API integrations, plus image generation.\n\n\n**Prioritizing UI Elements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the specific UI elements for this app. The goal is to design a user-friendly and functionally robust interface. Right now, I\'m concentrating on the hero banner with express delivery, curated catalog categories, and featured daily goods with live inventory. I\'m also addressing the interactive floating cart drawer with its delivery progress bar and item controls. I need to make sure the storefront and admin panels are easily accessible and seamlessly switchable.\n\n\n**Analyzing UI Interactions**\n\nI\'m now diving into the storefront UI in detail. I need to make sure I implement the category filtering, live search, cart features, and checkout. I\'m focusing on the floating cart drawer, delivery progress bar, and coupon code application. The admin and store operations portal, with inventory tracking, stock syncing, and sales analytics are my top priorities. I\'m concentrating on the seamless toggle between \"Admin Portal\" and \"Retail Storefront.\" I\'m also examining the uploaded images and provided HTML for available image resources, especially the exact URLs from the HTML.\n\n\n**Integrating Image Resources**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on incorporating the image assets. I\'ve successfully extracted the URLs for the profile picture, hero produce image, and the banana image. I\'m ready to begin integrating them into the app\'s UI elements.\n\n\n**Incorporating Image Assets**\n\nI\'ve acquired more image URLs for essential products: Milk, Apples, and a Sourdough loaf. Now I\'ll proceed with integrating these into the app.\n\n\n**Adding Product Images**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided product images. I\'ve successfully added the cold brew, avocados, Greek yogurt, and eggs carton to the app\'s catalog. The visual representation of the products is coming to life.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 96575567
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
