  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Component Requirements**\n\nI\'ve started breaking down the required components for the storefront. Specifically, I\'m focusing on `src/components/Header.tsx`, making sure to understand the logo, brand name, the \"Retail Storefront\" badge, and the location selector. My next focus is on implementing the search bar, making sure it integrates with the global search filter.\n\n\n**Expanding Header Functionality**\n\nI\'m now diving into the \"Header\" component, adding the \"Admin Portal\" button and the cart button. I need to make sure the cart displays a live count. I\'ll also add the user profile avatar and a dropdown with essential options. I will have to start on the secondary aisle navigation bar next, with dynamic active highlights.\n\n\n**Defining Product Listing Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the product listing components. I am exploring `src/components/CategoryGrid.tsx`, noting the need for category cards with dynamic icons, counts, and filtering. Next, I am thinking through `src/components/ProductCard.tsx`, paying attention to matching the design, like high-res images, stock badges, product titles, price details, and interactions. I\'ll need to figure out how to handle the stepper and \"Add\" button states. I must define the \"CartDrawer\" component details.\n\n\n**Detailing Checkout Components**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the checkout process, specifically the `CartDrawer` and `CheckoutModal` components. I am designing a delivery progress bar, item list, and coupon functionality. The `CheckoutModal` component will contain address input, payment options and order placement. I\'ll need to consider a real-time simulation. Further, I\'m thinking through a `ProductModal`, to show farm details, nutrition, and cold chain data. Finally, I\'ve got to consider the `AdminPortal`, and its store operation metrics, including SKU data.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 661984873
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
